DEBUG:docling.backend.md_backend: - RawText/Literal: sexual
DEBUG:docling.backend.md_backend: - RawText/Literal:  (gamete fusion) mechanisms. Asexual reproduction offers speed but little genetic diversity, while sexual reproduction—found in most plants and animals—generates variation essential for evolution. In plants, pollination, fertilization, and seed formation link the male and female structures of flowers. Animals display a wide range of reproductive strategies, from external fertilization in fish to internal gestation in mammals. Human reproduction follows a well‑coordinated hormonal cycle, culminating in fertilization, implantation, and development. Understanding the sources of genetic variation (crossing‑over, independent assortment, random fertilization, mutations) explains how species adapt and evolve.
